      "score": 98,
      "comments": 39,
      "author": "refp",
      "published": "2026-07-25T11:33:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "POSIX shell's `:` builtin returns exit status 0, providing a portable, zero-fork alternative to `true` in infinite loops like `while :`.",
        "Combine `:` with parameter expansion (e.g., `: \"${VAR:=default}\"`) to safely set default variables or evaluate expressions without executing commands.",
        "Utilize `: > file.txt` for fast, zero-fork file truncation, or as a readable POSIX-compliant no-op placeholder inside empty conditional branches."
      ]
